###  https://purl.archive.org/nudging#causal_matching_techniques
<https://purl.archive.org/nudging#causal_matching_techniques> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                       <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#Theory> ;
                                                              rdfs:comment "Propensity score matching (PSM):  is a common technique used to balance the two groups by creating pairs of individuals with similar socioeconomic characteristics (e.g., age, gender), one in the control group and one in the treatment group.  Coarsened Exact Matching (CEM) is more effective in reducing bias than PSM, as it categorizes variables into meaningful groups before comparing them. This method uses L1 distance (Manhattan distance) to measure imbalance between groups and improves balance by recoding continuous and discrete variables."@en ;
                                                              rdfs:label "casual matching techniques" .


