###  https://purl.archive.org/nudging#travel_behavior_determinants_in_built_environment
<https://purl.archive.org/nudging#travel_behavior_determinants_in_built_environment> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                              <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#Theory> ;
                                                                                     rdfs:comment "Vehicle-miles of travel (VMT) is most strongly related to destination accessibility, while walking is related to land use diversity, intersection density and the number of destinations within walking distance. Bus and train use are related to proximity to transit and street network design. Population and job densities are only weakly associated with travel behavior (TB) when the other 4Ds (density, diversity, design, destination accessibilty) are controlled."@en ;
                                                                                     rdfs:label "travel behaviour determinants in built environment" .


