###  https://purl.archive.org/nudging#3D_built_environment_theory
<https://purl.archive.org/nudging#3D_built_environment_theory> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                        <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/dul/DUL.owl#Theory> ;
                                                               rdfs:comment "Build Environment has originally been defined through the famous 3Ds of built environment: Density, Diversity, and Design, initially coined 1997 and since widely used in North American studies. 3D has grown to 5D with the addition of Destination accessibility and Distance to transit. Trip lengths are primarily a function of the Build Environment and secondarily of socioeconomics (SEC). Mode choices depend on both but probably more on SEC."@en ;
                                                               rdfs:label "3D built environment theory" .


